WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.930
Hi! How long is a pencil? How long is a classroom? Today we'll measure length in metres and centimetres.

2
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.538
For short things like a pencil or an eraser, use centimetres.

3
00:00:14.688 --> 00:00:19.194
For long things like a door's height or a classroom, use metres.

4
00:00:19.344 --> 00:00:22.698
1 metre is 100 centimetres.

5
00:00:22.848 --> 00:00:30.138
1 cm is about the width of your fingernail. 1 m is about your arms stretched out.

6
00:00:30.288 --> 00:00:34.530
Line up the 0 on the ruler with one end of the object.

7
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.754
Then read the number at the other end. That's the length.

8
00:00:38.904 --> 00:00:44.826
If it goes from 3 to 10, the length is 10 minus 3, which is 7 cm.

9
00:00:44.976 --> 00:00:49.218
Always write the unit after your answer.

10
00:00:49.368 --> 00:00:56.034
Watch out! 15 metres is longer than a classroom. A pencil can't be that long!

11
00:00:56.184 --> 00:01:01.194
A pencil is short, so use centimetres: 15 cm.

12
00:01:01.344 --> 00:01:06.306
After writing, ask: does this length make sense?

13
00:01:06.456 --> 00:01:16.482
Your turn! A door is about 2 what tall? Metres or centimetres? Pause and think.

14
00:01:16.632 --> 00:01:23.082
A door is taller than a person, about 2 metres. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:23.232 --> 00:01:31.962
Another one! How many centimetres are in 2 metres? Pause and think.

16
00:01:32.112 --> 00:01:40.170
1 m is 100 cm, so 2 m is 200 cm. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:50.970
Here's another! A ribbon goes from 4 to 13 on a ruler. How long is it? Pause and think.

18
00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:58.098
13 minus 4 is 9, so it's 9 cm. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:58.248 --> 00:02:10.866
Try one more! A rope is 85 cm. 30 cm is cut off. How much is left? Pause and think.

20
00:02:11.016 --> 00:02:19.626
85 minus 30 is 55. 55 cm is left. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:19.776 --> 00:02:32.418
Try one more! Two sticks are 45 cm and 38 cm. Joined end to end, how long are they? Pause and think.

22
00:02:32.568 --> 00:02:40.530
45 plus 38 is 83, so 83 cm. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:49.314
Last one! How many centimetres are in 2 metres? Pause and think.

24
00:02:49.464 --> 00:02:57.522
1 m is 100 cm, so 2 m is 200 cm. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:57.672 --> 00:03:09.138
Remember: use centimetres for short things and metres for long things. 1 m is 100 cm. Line up 0 with one end, and always write the unit.

26
00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:13.794
Measure your pencil and your desk today!

